       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **800 mg orally 4 times daily.** This is the 3,200 mg/day maximum, and it's a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg orally 4 times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg orally every 4\u20136 hours as needed** for analgesia or antipyresis.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it that way. If you want to enter one of the options above, tell me which one. I can also add a note, such as \"take with food.\""
      }
